-The implementation must prevent two concurrent attendants from successfully
-calling the same waiting ticket. The exact locking strategy belongs to the
-implementation and database transaction layer; the domain invariant is that a
-ticket can be called only once.
-
-> TODO (follow-up from review): link the test covering the single-call
-> invariant and concurrent-call protection once implemented.
+`App\Actions\CallNextTicket` is invokable, constructed without arguments, and
+receives `Queue $queue`, `User $calledBy` and an optional
+`CallMode $mode = CallMode::Any`. `App\Enums\CallMode` is string-backed:
+`any`, `priority_only`, `normal_only`. Inactive queues raise
+`App\Exceptions\InactiveQueueException`; a mode with no eligible waiting ticket
+raises `App\Exceptions\NoWaitingTicketsException`.
+
+Selection uses only `waiting` tickets of the passed queue. Full ordering is
+`priority` descending, then `issued_at` ascending, then `id` ascending.
+`priority_only` applies the same ordering but excludes normal tickets;
+`normal_only` excludes priority tickets and orders by `issued_at` then `id`.
+Fairness applies only to `any`: when the last three calls in the queue
+(ordered by `called_at` descending, then `id` descending) are all priority
+tickets and at least one normal is waiting, the call is restricted to the
+oldest normal ticket. Calls from every mode count in this history.
+
+Exactly-once is transactional. The action locks the queue row, re-reads its
+persisted state, selects a candidate, then locks the candidate row and
+re-checks its status before saving. `Ticket::call()` intentionally does not lock
+the queue, so a candidate may be called concurrently after selection; when
+that happens the action skips it and selects the next eligible ticket. Only
+`status`, `called_at` and `called_by_user_id` change, preserving the ticket's
+write-once rule. The action performs no authorization — the caller is trusted
+to enforce it at the boundary.
+
+Coverage: [`tests/Feature/CallNextTicketTest.php`](../tests/Feature/CallNextTicketTest.php)
+and the single-call invariant in
+[`tests/Feature/IssueTicketTest.php`](../tests/Feature/IssueTicketTest.php).
 
