+**Single-ticket call:** `Ticket::call()` marks one specific waiting ticket as `called` (entity-membership checked, exactly-once). It is the low-level primitive for an already chosen ticket; the attendant's call panel uses the call-next action below.
+
+**Call next:** domain action `App\Actions\CallNextTicket` implements the three call-panel buttons through `App\Enums\CallMode` (`any`, `priority_only`, `normal_only`). It only considers `waiting` tickets of the given queue, rejects inactive queues, and throws `App\Exceptions\NoWaitingTicketsException` when the requested mode has no eligible ticket. Selection is deterministic (priority, age, id) with the fairness rule below, and exactly one ticket is marked `called` per invocation. Authorization is the caller's responsibility; HTTP/Livewire panels remain out of scope.
 
